Summary:

Works out-of-the-box

Great for syntax, language, short code fixes

No access to your company policies or historical context

Mistral + LangChain + RAG (Contextual Architecture)
┌──────────────────────────┐
│        User Query        │
│ "Fix this YAML as per    │
│  our internal template"  │
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
  ┌───────────────────────────┐
  │     LangChain Pipeline    │
  │  - Structured prompt      │
  │  - Control flow / memory  │
  │  - Multi-step reasoning   │
  └────────────┬──────────────┘
               │
         (Retrieve Context)
               │
               ▼
     ┌───────────────────────────┐
     │    RAG Component          │
     │  - Vector DB (FAISS)      │
     │  - Internal DevOps docs   │
     │  - YAML / Terraform refs  │
     └────────────┬──────────────┘
                  │ (Context injected)
                  ▼
          ┌─────────────────┐
          │   Mistral LLM   │
          │ (Reason + Write)│
          └─────────────────┘
                  │
                  ▼
      Refined Output (corrected YAML + explanation)  
      Uses your org data  
      Follows internal standards


Summary:

LangChain acts as the orchestrator (prompt management, memory, pipeline logic)

RAG acts as the knowledge base (retrieves actual DevOps templates)

Mistral acts as the reasoning engine (final answer generation)

Task: “Fix this Deployment YAML using internal standards.”

Step	Mistral Alone	Mistral + LangChain + RAG
1️	Receives YAML	Receives YAML
2️	Generates corrected YAML from pretraining	Retrieves your “deployment_template.yaml”
3️	Suggests a valid syntax	Aligns with your org’s naming, replicas, ports
4️	No context for policies	Adds explanations and corrections per template
 Output	Generic YAML fix	Fully compliant YAML + Explanation
